<!-- [XPLAT] migrated from net48/WinForms — see MIGRATION_DOCS/TRANSITION_MAP.md -->
<!--
    [XPLAT] AgOpenGPS (GPS program) — live "Heading Chart" diagnostic (Avalonia view).

    1:1 visual PARITY reimplementation of the deleted WinForms Forms/Settings/FormGraphHeading
    (FormGraphHeading.cs + FormGraphHeading.Designer.cs). Per AAP §0.3.3 this is fidelity to the
    currently rendered Windows Forms UI, never a redesign: no new colors, no relayout, no UX change.

    The form shows two stacked live charts that compare the GPS course heading against the
    IMU-corrected heading, plus their running difference:
      * unoChart (top)    : "S"  = GPS heading (deg)            and "PWM" = IMU-corrected heading (deg)
      * rollChart (bottom): "Ro" = heading difference (deg)     and "Ze"  = constant zero baseline
    Three large readouts above the bottom chart print the current GPS heading, IMU heading and the
    signed difference.

    CHARTING RE-HOST (no new NuGet): the two Windows-only System.Windows.Forms.DataVisualization
    Chart controls are removed and re-hosted as custom Avalonia drawing — the same point-buffer plus
    Render(DrawingContext) polyline approach used by the sibling graph views (FormGraphSteerView /
    FormGraphXTEView). The actual polyline rendering is the deferred cross-platform charting work
    tracked in MIGRATION_DOCS/TRANSITION_MAP.md (CP4/CP9); this markup supplies the two black plot
    surfaces and the readout labels, and the partner code-behind owns the live drawing and data.

    WIRING CONTRACT — the partner code-behind FormGraphHeadingView.axaml.cs owns ALL behaviour,
    NOT this markup. This view is CODE-BEHIND DRIVEN: there is intentionally NO x:DataType, NO
    DataContext and NO {Binding} (mirroring the original imperative FormGraphHeading, which addressed
    its controls directly). The x:Name'd elements below are the entire integration surface and MUST
    keep these names so the generated typed fields match the code-behind:
      * unoChart  : top plot surface (black). The code-behind plots the "S" (GPS heading) and "PWM"
                    (IMU-corrected heading) series into it. Original series colors (copied verbatim
                    from FormGraphHeading.Designer.cs) — "S": LightSalmon line, magenta (255,128,255)
                    border, width 2, StepLine; "PWM": Lime, width 2, StepLine.
      * rollChart : bottom plot surface (black), fixed Y range −10..+10 with a grid interval of 2 in
                    the original. The code-behind plots "Ro" (heading difference) and "Ze" (zero
                    baseline) — "Ro": Cyan StepLine; "Ze": Red FastLine.
      * lblSteerAng / lblPWM / lblDiff : the live readouts. The code-behind sets their Text from
                    glm.toDegrees(mf.gpsHeading) / glm.toDegrees(mf.imuCorrected) ("N1") and the
                    signed difference ("N2"), formatted with CultureInfo.InvariantCulture exactly as
                    the WinForms DrawChart() did (invariant formatting is required for cross-platform
                    parity on comma-decimal locales).
      * It also runs the sample timer at the GPS rate (WinForms System.Windows.Forms.Timer ->
                    Avalonia DispatcherTimer, interval = 1000 / gpsHz ms) and keeps each series to a
                    rolling 100-point window, mirroring the original.

    WINDOW SHELL — mirrors FormGraphHeading.Designer.cs exactly:
      Text "Heading Chart"           -> Title (decorations are hidden; kept for parity/accessibility)
      ClientSize 495 x 470           -> Width / Height (SystemDecorations="None" => client == window)
      FormBorderStyle (fixed dialog) -> SystemDecorations="None" + CanResize="False"
      ShowInTaskbar = false          -> ShowInTaskbar="False"
      StartPosition.CenterParent     -> WindowStartupLocation="CenterOwner" (shown over FormGPS)
      Font "Tahoma"                  -> FontFamily="Tahoma" (children set explicit sizes below)

    THEME / PARITY NOTE: the WinForms form painted its chrome with a near-black system color
    (ActiveCaptionText) behind the two black charts. Per this file's specification the window chrome
    is bound to the app day/night frame brush — Background="{DynamicResource AogFrameBrush}" from
    App.axaml's ThemeDictionaries (DynamicResource so the live Light<->Dark switch is observed) —
    while the two plot surfaces stay explicitly Black, matching the original chart BackColor. The
    readout/legend colors are the exact System.Drawing colors from the designer, expressed as the
    equivalent Avalonia named colors.

    xmlns:gStr is declared per this view's specification for access to AgOpenGPS.Core.Translations;
    the legend captions ("Fix2Fix", "IMU") and axis ticks ("+10" / "0" / "-10") were plain literals
    in the WinForms designer (not localized resource keys), so they remain literals here for parity.
-->
<Window xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
        xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
        xmlns:gStr="clr-namespace:AgOpenGPS.Core.Translations;assembly=AgOpenGPS.Core"
        x:Class="AgOpenGPS.Views.Settings.FormGraphHeadingView"
        Title="Heading Chart"
        Width="495"
        Height="470"
        CanResize="False"
        ShowInTaskbar="False"
        SystemDecorations="None"
        WindowStartupLocation="CenterOwner"
        Background="{DynamicResource AogFrameBrush}"
        FontFamily="Tahoma">

    <!--
        Absolute-positioned overlay layout. The original form used fixed Control.Location /
        Control.Size coordinates and overlaps the readout labels on top of the charts, so a Canvas
        reproduces it pixel-for-pixel (the window is a fixed 495 x 470, CanResize="False").

        Z-ORDER: Avalonia paints Canvas children in declaration order (first = back, last = front).
        In the WinForms designer the charts were added LAST to Controls (i.e. back-most), with the
        labels in front; so the two plot surfaces are declared FIRST here and every label AFTER them,
        guaranteeing the readouts paint on top of the charts exactly as before.
    -->
    <Canvas>

        <!-- ===================== Plot surfaces (custom-drawn, black) ===================== -->

        <!-- unoChart: WinForms Chart @ Location (3,3) Size 487 x 126, BackColor Black. Hosts the
             "S" (GPS heading) and "PWM" (IMU-corrected heading) series. The code-behind fills this
             surface with the custom polyline drawing; ClipToBounds keeps the plot inside the rect
             just as the WinForms ChartArea clipped its series. -->
        <Border x:Name="unoChart"
                Canvas.Left="3"
                Canvas.Top="3"
                Width="487"
                Height="126"
                Background="Black"
                ClipToBounds="True" />

        <!-- rollChart: WinForms Chart @ Location (9,129) Size 481 x 342, BackColor Black, fixed
             Y axis −10..+10 (grid interval 2). Hosts the "Ro" (heading difference) and "Ze" (zero
             baseline) series, drawn by the code-behind. -->
        <Border x:Name="rollChart"
                Canvas.Left="9"
                Canvas.Top="129"
                Width="481"
                Height="342"
                Background="Black"
                ClipToBounds="True" />

        <!-- ===================== Live readouts (overlaid on top chart) ===================== -->

        <!-- lblSteerAng: GPS heading value. WinForms Label @ (110,100) 85 x 29, Tahoma 18pt Bold
             (18pt * 96/72 = 24 DIP), ForeColor OrangeRed on a black box (BackColor ControlText),
             text MiddleLeft. Text assigned by the code-behind ("N1", InvariantCulture). -->
        <TextBlock x:Name="lblSteerAng"
                   Canvas.Left="110"
                   Canvas.Top="100"
                   Width="85"
                   Height="29"
                   Background="Black"
                   Foreground="OrangeRed"
                   FontSize="24"
                   FontWeight="Bold"
                   TextAlignment="Left"
                   VerticalAlignment="Center"
                   Text="0" />

        <!-- lblPWM: IMU-corrected heading value. WinForms Label @ (276,100) 85 x 29, Tahoma 18pt
             Bold, ForeColor Lime on black, MiddleLeft. Text assigned by the code-behind ("N1"). -->
        <TextBlock x:Name="lblPWM"
                   Canvas.Left="276"
                   Canvas.Top="100"
                   Width="85"
                   Height="29"
                   Background="Black"
                   Foreground="Lime"
                   FontSize="24"
                   FontWeight="Bold"
                   TextAlignment="Left"
                   VerticalAlignment="Center"
                   Text="0" />

        <!-- lblDiff: signed GPS-minus-IMU heading difference. WinForms Label @ (387,100) 85 x 29,
             Tahoma 18pt Bold, ForeColor Cyan on black, MiddleLeft. Text assigned by the code-behind
             ("N2", InvariantCulture). -->
        <TextBlock x:Name="lblDiff"
                   Canvas.Left="387"
                   Canvas.Top="100"
                   Width="85"
                   Height="29"
                   Background="Black"
                   Foreground="Cyan"
                   FontSize="24"
                   FontWeight="Bold"
                   TextAlignment="Left"
                   VerticalAlignment="Center"
                   Text="0" />

        <!-- ===================== Static legend / axis captions ===================== -->

        <!-- label1 "Fix2Fix": legend for the GPS-heading readout. WinForms Label @ (38,104) 74 x 23,
             Tahoma 14.25pt (= 19 DIP), ForeColor OrangeRed, MiddleRight. -->
        <TextBlock Canvas.Left="38"
                   Canvas.Top="104"
                   Width="74"
                   Height="23"
                   Background="Black"
                   Foreground="OrangeRed"
                   FontSize="19"
                   TextAlignment="Right"
                   VerticalAlignment="Center"
                   Text="Fix2Fix" />

        <!-- label5 "IMU": legend for the IMU-heading readout. WinForms Label @ (223,104) 55 x 23,
             Tahoma 14.25pt, ForeColor Chartreuse, MiddleRight. -->
        <TextBlock Canvas.Left="223"
                   Canvas.Top="104"
                   Width="55"
                   Height="23"
                   Background="Black"
                   Foreground="Chartreuse"
                   FontSize="19"
                   TextAlignment="Right"
                   VerticalAlignment="Center"
                   Text="IMU" />

        <!-- label2 "+10": top Y-axis tick of the roll chart. WinForms Label @ (-2,142) 44 x 23,
             Tahoma 14.25pt, ForeColor white (ButtonHighlight), MiddleRight. -->
        <TextBlock Canvas.Left="-2"
                   Canvas.Top="142"
                   Width="44"
                   Height="23"
                   Background="Black"
                   Foreground="White"
                   FontSize="19"
                   TextAlignment="Right"
                   VerticalAlignment="Center"
                   Text="+10" />

        <!-- label4 "0": mid Y-axis tick of the roll chart. WinForms Label @ (12,273) 20 x 23,
             Tahoma 14.25pt, ForeColor white, MiddleRight. -->
        <TextBlock Canvas.Left="12"
                   Canvas.Top="273"
                   Width="20"
                   Height="23"
                   Background="Black"
                   Foreground="White"
                   FontSize="19"
                   TextAlignment="Right"
                   VerticalAlignment="Center"
                   Text="0" />

        <!-- label3 "-10": bottom Y-axis tick of the roll chart. WinForms Label @ (5,425) 37 x 23,
             Tahoma 14.25pt, ForeColor white, MiddleRight. -->
        <TextBlock Canvas.Left="5"
                   Canvas.Top="425"
                   Width="37"
                   Height="23"
                   Background="Black"
                   Foreground="White"
                   FontSize="19"
                   TextAlignment="Right"
                   VerticalAlignment="Center"
                   Text="-10" />

    </Canvas>
</Window>
